  "readmeFile": "nuget.md",
  "releaseNotes": "11.0.1\n\n* Fixed: bom (the first day of the month) was read and documented but never acted on, in any\n  version. A task with bom set to true ran every day. It now runs on the 1st only. If a task of\n  yours has bom and you came to rely on it running daily, take the tag out.\n* New: IHTaskControlProperties.FirstDayOfMonth, which is what the engine now looks at. It has a\n  default (null), so your own implementation of the interface still compiles and loads unchanged.\n\n11.0.0\n\nA task whose handler throws is handled differently. If you relied on a failing task being tried\nagain every second, set sleep_on_error to your tick interval.\n\n* New: a net11.0 build, for .NET 11. The net8.0, net9.0 and net10.0 builds stay. The major version\n  is 11 because it follows the .NET generation, and the package now depends on Com.H 11.0.x.\n* Fixed: a task that threw was tried again on every tick (every second by default), whatever its\n  schedule, unless both retry_attempts_on_error and sleep_on_error were set. It now waits before\n  the next try: for sleep_on_error if set, otherwise for its interval, otherwise for\n  HTaskScheduler.DefaultSleepOnError (new, 60 seconds).\n* Fixed: sleep_on_error was ignored without retry_attempts_on_error.\n* Fixed: a task that used up its retry_attempts_on_error did not run again (a task that had never\n  succeeded: not until its XML changed). It now waits for its next scheduled time and starts it\n  with a full count. retry_attempts_on_error 0 means no retries.\n* Fixed: a task that last ran before today and failed today lost its retry count and the time of\n  its last error on every save of the log, so its retry settings had no effect.\n* Changed: an exception from a handler is reported through TaskExecutionError and nowhere else,\n  with or without retry settings. Before, without retry_attempts_on_error it was also rethrown,\n  from a task that nothing awaits.\n* Fixed: a handler stopped by the scheduler's own shutdown was counted as a failure.\n* Fixed: the constructor taking an IHTaskCollection threw on start, for want of a config path.\n* New: HTaskScheduler.ValueProcessors registers custom value processors before the start.",
